# atomic sandbox scene v1
# Phosphine: P-H 1.421 Angstrom (2.6853 Bohr), H-P-H 93.3 degrees (C3v, apex up). NIST CCCBDB, experimental geometry
# (rPH, aHPH; Herzberg, Electronic spectra and electronic structure of polyatomic molecules, 1966), converted at
# 1 Angstrom = 1.8897261 Bohr; the H sit 1.4584 Bohr below the P.
# The file carries no `ionic` line (the presets are the files as written): the app starts it under its default
# policy, cores only, where the Z > 10 atom is a generated pseudopotential on its valence grid. Under
# `--ionic none` the heavy nucleus is a Gaussian at sigma = h (Z sigma ~ 2.3 at h = 0.15): qualitatively wrong, not a
# useful run. 14 Bohr box at 57 x 0.25 as written (the Accurate default re-grids it to 95^3 x 0.15, same box).
grid 57 0.25
charge 0
nucleus 15  0       0      0
nucleus 1   2.2548  0     -1.4584
nucleus 1  -1.1274  1.9527 -1.4584
nucleus 1  -1.1274 -1.9527 -1.4584
